(EXP-96: LANGUAGE.md:2167 - text to number "fails if text is not a valid number
 and sets the error flag". True only when NOTHING parses. A string with a valid
 prefix parses that prefix and leaves the flag clear. See Discrepancy 2.
 `On error` binds to the statement before it, so each handler here sits
 directly under the cast it is judging.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox EXP-96.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   fully invalid base 10 set the flag
   0
   12
   empty string set the flag
   0
)
a text called rubbish is "abc".
a number called 'from rubbish' is rubbish as a number.
On error Print "fully invalid base 10 set the flag".
Print 'from rubbish'.
a text called partial is "12xy".
a number called 'from partial' is partial as a number.
On error Print "partial base 10 set the flag".
Print 'from partial'.
a text called blank is "".
a number called 'from blank' is blank as a number.
On error Print "empty string set the flag".
Print 'from blank'.
